### Step 3: Compute the coordinates of the vertices

Let’s define the rotation matrix again:

$$
R = \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \\
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

Let’s compute the vectors step by step.

#### First side:
$$
v_1 = (1, 0)
$$

#### Second side:
$$
v_2 = a_2 \cdot R(v_1) = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \\
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
\cdot (1, 0) = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \\
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

#### Third side:
$$
v_3 = a_3 \cdot R(v_2) = 1 \cdot R\left(\begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}\right)
$$

Compute $R \cdot \begin{bmatrix} -\frac{1}{2} \\ \frac{1}{2} \end{bmatrix}$:

$$
R \cdot \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot (-\frac{1}{2}) - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot \frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot (-\frac{1}{2}) - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot \frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} \\
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{4}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

So:

$$
v_3 = \begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

#### Fourth side:
$$
v_4 = a_4 \cdot R(v_3) = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot R\left(\begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}\right)
$$

Compute $R \cdot \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \end{bmatrix}$:

$$
R \cdot \begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot 0 - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot (-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot 0 - \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot (-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2})
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

So:

$$
v_4 = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \cdot \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{1}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{4} \\
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{4}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

